{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FesBPSGmKUN6e9YtE5tRgf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The AAAI review scale goes from 1 to 8 based on the statistics. Let me look for the specific AAAI review form. AAAI typically uses the following scale:\n\nBased on my knowledge, AAAI typically uses:\n- Overall recommendation: 1-10 scale\n  - 10: Strong Accept\n  - 9: Accept  \n  - 8: Accept\n  - 7: Weak Accept\n  - 6: Weak Accept / Borderline Accept\n  - 5: Borderline / Weak Reject\n  - 4: Reject\n  - 3: Reject\n  - 2: Strong Reject\n  - 1: Strong Reject\n\nBut the AAAI 2025 statistics show a range of 1-8, so it looks like they've shifted to an 8-point scale. Looking at recent conferences, AAAI-25 and AAAI-26 appear to use this mapping: 1 for Strong Reject through 8 for Strong Accept, with the middle values representing various degrees of borderline and weak recommendations.\n\nThough I'm also seeing references to a 1-10 scale where 10 represents top-tier papers and 1 represents trivial or incorrect work. The PaperCopilot data specifically shows 1-8 for AAAI 2025, so there's a discrepancy I need to resolve about which scale is actually being used. I'm searching more specifically for the AAAI review form to confirm the exact scoring scale they use.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":830,"cache_read_input_tokens":55815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":830},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44955cf6-fbf6-481a-ac64-bdae83b1911e","uuid":"74a00998-0b27-47e4-8c23-fb13dd63bf35"}
